1:# Proposed ZKIRv4 and Midnight recursion requirements
3:Status: explicit proposed interface contract, specified-only. Owner: joint Midnight backend / Moriarty integration work. Date: 2026-09-19. The user expects comprehensive Midnight recursion in about six months, approximately March 2027. This is the planning horizon for the full architecture, not an independently verified release date. Current execution targets ZKIRv3. Following the user’s documentation request, ZKIRv4 names the proposed next-version requirements workstream here; it does not assert an announced or released upstream version.
5:These requirements make the platform dependency actionable. They request comprehensive native recursion for developer-defined relations, portable compliance and private bounded multi-parent composition—not merely proof aggregation. No Lean dependency or alternate proof backend is introduced. [Unified roadmap](../ROADMAP.md): U0 adopts this versioned requested contract; U1/U4 reconcile it with the released compatible tuple without silently weakening mandatory scope; U1 investigates compatibility/cost; U2 integrates current supported paths; U4 qualifies full recursion/private composition; U5 qualifies external adapters. No current limitation permanently narrows that target.
7:“SHALL” below states the requested behavior. All acceptance tests are specified, not executed by this design work. Cryptographic soundness and correspondence need arguments as well as tests. Performance targets remain unquantified until measurements support them; no arbitrary latency or proof-size promise is imposed.
15:| ZR01 — C, versioned interface | The native interface SHALL identify the exact ZKIR instruction semantics, compiler/lowerer, proof format, transcript, circuit/VK, SRS provenance, accumulator/decider format and ledger verifier versions required by an artifact. Unsupported combinations SHALL fail closed before financial acceptance. | Compatible tuple proves/verifies; change one version, transcript or serialization identifier and obtain explicit rejection. Retained artifacts verify in an independently installed compatible verifier. | Separate local pins and the historical contract/inner transcript mismatch are known; a comprehensive compatible release tuple is unknown. |
16:| ZR02 — C, general program relations | The interface SHALL support recursively composing proofs of developer-defined bounded relations expressible in the supported ZKIR profile, including both same-relation steps and explicitly compatible different-relation steps, without a maintainer program allowlist. | Independently author a new two-asset relation outside loan/swap fixtures; prove two steps. Compose compatible heterogeneous steps; reject a wrong relation with otherwise valid proof bytes. | MPS-0014 proposes same/cross-circuit composition. General Moriarty native capability is unestablished. |
17:| ZR03 — C, complete statement binding | Recursive verification SHALL bind canonical public inputs or binding commitments for program/semantics, property, signed intent, domain, predecessors, observations, complete effects, residual duties and resource limits; the application circuit SHALL enforce equality within the same canonical representation and pinned correspondence/refinement links where source, Core, ZKIR and ledger representations differ. Distinct representation hashes are expected; their authorized linkage is enforced. | Mutate each component individually while retaining other valid objects: every unauthorized mismatch of identity or its correspondence linkage rejects; mere inequality of different representation hashes is not a failure. Authorized witness variation and alternative permitted routes remain valid. | Ordinary proof input machinery exists, but this complete Moriarty statement and correspondence are open. |
18:| ZR04 — C, genesis and well-foundedness | A recursive compliance relation SHALL distinguish legitimate base cases from recursive cases and enforce well-founded descent or an equivalent sound induction structure; genesis funding, authority and initialization SHALL be authenticated. | Valid funded base and descendants verify; fabricated funded/approved genesis, recursive proof relabeled base, cycle and rank-wraparound reject. Require a soundness argument, not only finite tests. | An IVC example exists; application genesis and general sequence/DAG theorem are unestablished. A rank counter is one choice, not mandated syntax. |
19:| ZR05 — C, verifier identity | Every verified predecessor SHALL use a VK/relation identity authorized by the bound program policy, including any accumulator state and decider identity; a prover SHALL NOT select a weaker relation by substituting a key. | Proof of a trivial true circuit, wrong VK, wrong decider, stale compatible-looking module or substituted IVC state identity rejects. Explicitly authorized compatible module succeeds. | Historical PR738 described pinned inner-key hashes and a Collapsed-state hazard; current fix/deployment status unknown. Fixed keys and policy-checked dynamic keys are alternative realizations. |
20:| ZR06 — C, adversarial-witness soundness | For the supported profile, satisfaction of target constraints SHALL imply a valid semantic realization for every accepted witness, including type/range, Boolean, inactive-branch, encoding and output-shape premises. Honest-witness preprocessing SHALL NOT be the sole enforcement of such premises. | Prove the implication; challenge non-Boolean selectors/assertions, out-of-width comparisons, noncanonical encodings, unconstrained outputs and altered inactive-branch values where semantically material. Valid boundary values must remain accepted. | Explicit preconditions and constraint operations are visible locally. PR17's WShape premise remains conditional evidence, not blanket target soundness. |
21:| ZR07 — C, mandatory verification/control | The application relation SHALL ensure every mandatory predecessor and intention predicate constrains acceptance, including verification guards and all supported branches. An inactive verifier SHALL NOT satisfy an obligation for an active predecessor. | Set verification guard to zero, discard a computed false result, omit one required parent, or route through a failure branch that bypasses mandatory checks: reject. A deliberately optional inactive parent follows its specified semantics. | Historical PR738 allowed guard-based disabling. Safe application dominance and actual current lowering remain unestablished. This does not prohibit useful optional guards. |
22:| ZR08 — C, complete deferred verification | Before financial acceptance, the native verifier/ledger SHALL discharge every deferred cryptographic obligation necessary for the recursive statement, including all accumulators and final pairing/decider checks, binding them to the outer statement. No API SHALL report final validity after only the outer proof check when obligations remain. | Use a well-formed but invalid inner proof and a valid proof for the wrong instance that still permit outer proof construction; final verification rejects both. Dropped/substituted accumulators, semantic mismatches caused by reordering, and bypass paths reject; sound order-insensitive batching remains permitted. | Frozen September 11 evidence reports the accumulator pairing caught such cases in a PR test. Production/native general integration unknown. Separate or safely batched checks are both acceptable. |
23:| ZR09 — C, bounded multi-parent joins | The interface SHALL support a declared bounded number of predecessor proofs, at least two for MC06, and the application join relation SHALL enforce predecessor compatibility, resource partition/recombination, complete duties and aggregate budgets without double-counting common ancestry. The per-stage fan-in bound does not impose a single fixed global DAG depth; growing finite well-founded histories preserve declared episode/lifetime budgets through authorized continuation. | Split, advance two branches and join; reject duplicated spendable parent, missing branch duty, incompatible intent/domain, and cumulative-budget duplication. Harmless shared ancestry is accepted when correctly accounted. | General bounded joins and their full financial relation are open. Repeated verification instructions or a dedicated join primitive are alternative implementations. |
24:| ZR10 — C, state and ledger consumption | Native acceptance SHALL bind proved predecessor/resource identities to authenticated current ledger state and enforce the declared unique-consumption/nonce rules; imported certificates SHALL carry an authenticated anchor and cannot manufacture currentness. | Race two valid successors of one spendable state; at most one consumes it. Reject stale head, absent-head creation without authenticated absence, replay across domains and unrecognized anchor. | Historical ledger read validation is relevant evidence; the complete recursion/consumption integration is unestablished. Proof validity alone cannot provide this property. |
25:| ZR11 — C, compiler/effect correspondence | The compiler and accepted native statement SHALL preserve source stage results, rejection, exact arithmetic, effects and residual state, including guaranteed/fallible phase layout and every permitted retained-fee outcome. | Two-phase case with failed fallible business action: recorded guaranteed effects/fees match signed policy, nonce and duties. Unauthorized fee, missing liability or invented rollback rejects. Prove arbitrary-accepted-witness correspondence for the supported slice. | Source/5 and restricted Compact paths exist separately; full source/native/ledger relation is open. New ZKIR opcodes are not intrinsically required if existing constraints suffice. |
