28:| ZR14 — C, private continuation interface | The recursive interface SHALL permit statements over binding private-state commitments with proved consistency, and tooling SHALL identify precisely which witness/proof/key artifacts a separately controlled successor needs. Claimed privacy SHALL name observers and leakage; proof reuse SHALL NOT be advertised as delivery of hidden state. | Separate Alice/Bob environments perform supported continuation and split/join without unauthorized secret access; missing witness data surfaces as unavailable, not a fabricated proof. Prove/assess declared confidentiality separately. | Native ZK is a foundation, not a private handoff theorem. MC06's separate-party witness and privacy obligations remain open. MPC is one possible provider with explicit assumptions, not a mandatory backend replacement. |
