raw/assignments/moriarty-typescript-elm-unison-research-2026-09-09.md:7:Scope interpretation: a separate research branch acquires public primary papers and official Elm/Unison documentation, retains exact source captures and provenance, and develops a source-grounded feature checklist. TypeScript-style syntax and Midnight Compact targeting are constraints. Functional-reactive mechanisms and content addressing are proposals to assess against finite execution, units, residual duties, explicit authority/effects and source/Core/K/Compact/ledger obligations. This request does not admit unrestricted TypeScript execution or freeze new language semantics.
raw/assignments/moriarty-typescript-elm-unison-research-2026-09-09.md:11:The later user instruction replaces Claude Fable review with Opus. The controlling record is [the Opus reviewer override](moriarty-opus-review-routing-2026-09-09.md), published on main by the parent stream. Until main is integrated into this branch, that target may not exist locally; the current user instruction still controls. Preserve actual resolved reviewer identities. The additive README small-step-semantics request is handled separately by the parent stream.
raw/assignments/moriarty-pcd-report-steering-2026-09-06.md:11:> we also have recursion and halo2 available via midnight
raw/assignments/moriarty-pcd-report-steering-2026-09-06.md:14:the user's requirement for bounded semantics, ACTUS/DeFi targets and mandatory
raw/assignments/moriarty-pcd-report-steering-2026-09-06.md:17:language recursion rules.
raw/assignments/moriarty-target-first-reset-2026-09-06.md:22:implementation targets. Absence of those targets was not the cause of the detour.
raw/assignments/moriarty-twelve-sprint-afk-execution-2026-09-07.md:9:The selected Midnight target, mandatory PCD, bounded language, financial coverage and factual acceptance predicates remain required. Majority decisions choose design and resource actions; they cannot turn a failed proof/test into passing evidence. Current independent implementation/result reviews remain required. Preserve historical charges and admit bounded successor allocations before actionful campaigns. This file is authority, not evidence that a loop is running.
raw/assignments/moriarty-completion-loop-2026-09-07.md:12:>   - [ ] Produce a real native recursive proof. Blocked: the current R3 experiment exhausted rows at k17; review the encoding/resource
raw/assignments/moriarty-completion-loop-2026-09-07.md:25:It retains the ACTUS/DeFi target-first reset and Preview steering.
raw/assignments/moriarty-midnight-milestone-testing-2026-09-07.md:7:This steers the active twelve-sprint Grok4.6 high implementation and independent GPT6 review. Preview remains the sole public target. Test network-facing milestones using actual submitted transactions, finalized receipts, full state/effect comparisons, rejection controls and current deployed artifact identities. Local simulation, skip-zk compilation and source review do not substitute for network milestone evidence.
raw/assignments/moriarty-midnight-transaction-reporting-2026-09-07.md:7:For every Midnight blockchain submission made during this work, post the transaction ID in the conversation with its observed status. Distinguish submission from finalized success. Report failed or pending submissions too when an ID exists. Preserve the transaction and finalization receipts in the repository under the applicable campaign. This instruction does not change Preview-only targeting or milestone acceptance predicates. Git commit hashes are not blockchain transaction IDs.
raw/assignments/moriarty-autonomous-execution-2026-09-07.md:13:No change to proof semantics, financial target coverage or completion evidence follows from this delegation.
raw/assignments/moriarty-report-reconciliation-2026-09-07.md:7:Scope: review the exact documents, preserve provenance, graph their concepts and requirements, reconcile conflicts and evaluate the remaining Moriarty plan. Existing bounded, target-first, mandatory-PCD and Preview requirements remain controlling. A report is source material, not an instruction to change the product target.
raw/assignments/moriarty-report-reconciliation-2026-09-07.md:13:Midnight is the language implementation target. Other-chain material is comparative research and financial behavior input, not a multi-backend product roadmap. Compact, Midnight native proofs, private state and ledger acceptance constrain language design.
